      "stdout": "Add a global picture-adjust segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --brightness TEXT   Brightness, e.g. 0.3. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --contrast TEXT     Contrast. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --saturation TEXT   Saturation. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --color-temperature TEXT \r\n                              Color temperature. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --highlight TEXT    Highlight. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --shadow TEXT       Shadow. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --sharpening TEXT   Sharpening. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --resource TEXT     Adjust resource: vimo://<id> / local://<path>\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: at least one adjust field (e.g. --brightness) is required.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Brighten and add contrast to the whole picture-adjust layer\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft adjust add --brightness 0.3 --contrast 0.2\r\n  # Tune color/light fields together (saturation, temperature, highlight, shadow, sharpening)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft adjust add --saturation 0.2 --color-temperature 0.1 \\\r\n      --highlight 0.15 --shadow -0.1 --sharpening 0.3\r\n  # Place the adjust layer on a specific track and time range from a resource\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft adjust add --brightness 0.2 --track 1 --start 0s --duration 3s \\\r\n      --resource vimo://123\r\n",
